Package: zhiyi-ime
Version: @PROJECT_VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ZHIYI_DEB_ARCH@
Installed-Size: @ZHIYI_INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @ZHIYI_FRAMEWORK_DEPS@, libc6 (>= 2.14), libstdc++6 (>= 5.2),
 python3, python3-gi, python3-dbus, gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1
Maintainer: Zhiyi IME Linux port <zhiyi-ime@localhost>
Homepage: https://github.com/dd1000001000/zhiyi_ime
Description: Zhiyi Pinyin input method for Fcitx (Linux port)
 Linux port of the Windows Zhiyi IME. Reuses the upstream 1.46-million-entry
 pinyin lexicon and shuangpin schemas. Ships input method addons for both
 Fcitx 4 and Fcitx 5; the build automatically produces the front end(s) the
 host framework(s) support, with identical engine behavior either way.
 .
 Supports full pinyin, initials abbreviations, fuzzy pinyin, five shuangpin
 schemes, sentence composition, Chinese punctuation and user dictionary
 learning. Configuration is handled by the zhiyi-config command and the
 zhiyi-tray settings menu (all options, including skin switching).
